Compiles clean. Now each run writes two files with matching timestamps to `results/`:

- `scorecard-<runLabel>-<timestamp>.csv` — unchanged, the per-question score rows
- `report-<runLabel>-<timestamp>.txt` — new, the same detailed report that prints to console (per-question Q/A, judge rationale, category averages, overall summary)

Whenever you run the benchmark yourself, both will land side by side so you can review the judging without having to scroll back through terminal output.